WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.950
Smallville Arrival

00:03.000 --> 00:07.000
Based on a novelisation by Michael Taitelbaum

00:20.000 --> 00:21.000
Arrival

00:22.000 --> 00:26.000
Chapter 1 A child arrives

00:27.000 --> 00:32.000
1989 Smallville, Kansas, USA

00:33.000 --> 00:35.950
Suddenly the sky was dark

00:36.000 --> 00:38.950
There were hundreds of meteors in the sky

00:39.000 --> 00:42.000
They went faster and faster

00:43.000 --> 00:47.000
There was a very small spaceship in the centre of the meteors

00:48.000 --> 00:50.950
There was one person in this spaceship

00:51.000 --> 00:53.000
A child

00:54.000 --> 00:56.950
Nothing happened in Smallville

00:57.000 --> 00:59.950
It was a small town in Kansas

01:00.000 --> 01:02.950
And it was a very boring place

01:03.000 --> 01:07.000
Then one day everything changed

01:08.000 --> 01:12.950
Lionel Luther arrived from Metropolis in his helicopter

01:13.000 --> 01:14.950
He was a rich man

01:15.000 --> 01:16.950
But he was not a nice man

01:17.000 --> 01:20.000
He loved money, not people

01:21.000 --> 01:23.950
His young son Lex sat next to him

01:24.000 --> 01:26.950
Lex was nine years old

01:27.000 --> 01:29.950
He had red hair and blue eyes

01:30.000 --> 01:31.950
His face was white

01:32.000 --> 01:33.950
And his eyes were closed

01:34.000 --> 01:36.000
He was very frightened

01:37.000 --> 01:39.950
Lex shouted his father

01:40.000 --> 01:41.950
Open your eyes now

01:42.000 --> 01:43.950
I can't

01:44.000 --> 01:44.950
Lex said

01:45.000 --> 01:47.000
I hate this helicopter

01:48.000 --> 01:50.950
Luther's aren't frightened of anything

01:51.000 --> 01:51.950
Lionel said

01:52.000 --> 01:55.000
Look out of the window now

01:57.000 --> 01:59.950
Lex slowly opened his eyes and looked down

02:00.000 --> 02:01.950
I'm going to die

02:02.000 --> 02:04.000
He thought

02:05.000 --> 02:08.950
Two men waited for the helicopter in the car park of an old factory

02:09.000 --> 02:11.950
The men were brothers

02:12.000 --> 02:14.000
Dale and Bill Ross

02:15.000 --> 02:18.950
Why does Lionel Luther want to buy our factory?

02:19.000 --> 02:20.950
Ask Dale

02:21.000 --> 02:22.950
I don't know, said Bill

02:23.000 --> 02:25.950
But we need his money

02:26.000 --> 02:27.950
He isn't going to change anything

02:28.000 --> 02:32.000
He told us that And I believe him

02:33.000 --> 02:35.950
Jonathan Kent and his wife Martha

02:36.000 --> 02:38.950
went into a shop on Main Street

02:39.000 --> 02:41.950
Their faces were brown from the sun

02:42.000 --> 02:43.950
And their jeans were old

02:44.000 --> 02:45.950
They lived on a farm

02:46.000 --> 02:47.950
Afternoon, Nell

02:48.000 --> 02:49.950
Jonathan said

02:50.000 --> 02:51.950
Hello, Jonathan

02:52.000 --> 02:52.950
Nell said

02:53.000 --> 02:53.950
She smiled at him

02:54.000 --> 02:55.950
She liked Jonathan

02:56.000 --> 02:57.950
Hello, Martha

02:58.000 --> 02:59.950
She said

03:00.000 --> 03:01.950
She didn't smile at Martha

03:02.000 --> 03:05.950
She didn't like her I'd like some tulips

03:06.000 --> 03:07.950
Said Martha

03:08.000 --> 03:10.000
Red tulips, please

03:12.000 --> 03:13.950
There was a little girl in the shop

03:14.000 --> 03:15.950
She was very pretty with dark hair

03:16.000 --> 03:18.000
She was three years old

03:20.000 --> 03:21.950
Hello, Lana

03:22.000 --> 03:23.950
Said Martha

03:24.000 --> 03:25.950
Where are your mum and dad today?

03:26.000 --> 03:27.950
They're at the homecoming game

03:28.000 --> 03:29.950
Nell said

03:30.000 --> 03:31.950
Here are your tulips

03:32.000 --> 03:33.950
She gave them to Jonathan

03:34.000 --> 03:35.950
In the street

03:36.000 --> 03:37.950
Martha said sadly

03:38.000 --> 03:39.950
Oh, Jonathan

03:40.000 --> 03:41.950
I looked at Lana's little face

03:42.000 --> 03:43.950
And I

03:44.000 --> 03:45.950
She stopped

03:46.000 --> 03:47.950
I know Martha

03:48.000 --> 03:49.950
Said Jonathan

03:50.000 --> 03:51.950
We both want a child

03:52.000 --> 03:55.950
The meteors came closer and closer

03:56.000 --> 03:57.950
At the factory

03:58.000 --> 03:59.950
Lex was bored

04:00.000 --> 04:01.950
He walked away into a cornfield

04:02.000 --> 04:03.950
Next to the factory

04:04.000 --> 04:05.950
Lionel Luther read the papers

04:06.000 --> 04:07.950
Where do I put my name?

04:08.000 --> 04:09.950
He asked the Ross brothers

04:10.000 --> 04:11.950
He smiled

04:12.000 --> 04:15.950
The factory was his now

04:16.000 --> 04:17.950
Alone in the field

04:18.000 --> 04:19.950
Lex suddenly heard something

04:20.000 --> 04:21.950
Help me

04:22.000 --> 04:23.950
What was it?

04:24.000 --> 04:25.950
Then he heard it again

04:26.000 --> 04:27.950
Help me

04:28.000 --> 04:29.950
He walked through the corn

04:30.000 --> 04:31.950
And suddenly

04:32.000 --> 04:33.950
There was a scarecrow

04:34.000 --> 04:35.950
Lex was frightened

04:36.000 --> 04:37.950
Lex was frightened

04:38.000 --> 04:39.950
That scarecrow can talk

04:40.000 --> 04:41.950
He thought

04:42.000 --> 04:43.950
But then it wasn't a scarecrow

04:44.000 --> 04:45.950
It was a teenage boy

04:46.000 --> 04:49.950
The boy was on a big wooden pole

04:50.000 --> 04:51.950
He had no shirt

04:52.000 --> 04:55.950
There was a big red S on the front of his body

04:56.000 --> 04:57.950
Help me

04:58.000 --> 04:59.950
Please

05:00.000 --> 05:01.950
He said one more time

05:02.000 --> 05:03.950
Boom

05:04.000 --> 05:05.950
A big meteor

05:06.000 --> 05:07.950
Crashed into the cornfield

05:08.000 --> 05:09.950
Lex ran

05:10.000 --> 05:11.950
A car

05:12.000 --> 05:13.950
Stopped opposite Nell's shop on Main Street

05:14.000 --> 05:15.950
Nell took little Lana in her arms

05:16.000 --> 05:17.950
And walked out of the shop

05:18.000 --> 05:21.950
Lewis and Laura Lang were in the car

05:22.000 --> 05:23.950
Lana saw them

05:24.000 --> 05:25.950
Mommy, daddy

05:26.000 --> 05:27.950
She shouted

05:28.000 --> 05:29.950
Nell looked up

05:30.000 --> 05:32.000
And saw a big meteor in the sky

05:33.000 --> 05:34.950
Doom

05:35.000 --> 05:38.950
The meteor crashed into the Lang's car

05:39.000 --> 05:42.950
Lana's parents were dead

05:43.000 --> 05:45.950
Lionel Luther ran across the cornfield

05:46.000 --> 05:47.950
Lex, where are you?

05:48.000 --> 05:49.950
He shouted

05:50.000 --> 05:52.950
He saw some red hair on the ground

05:53.000 --> 05:55.950
Then he found his son

05:56.000 --> 05:57.950
Lex was on the ground

05:58.000 --> 05:59.950
He was very frightened

06:00.000 --> 06:02.950
But where was his beautiful red hair?

06:03.000 --> 06:04.950
He was nine years old

06:05.000 --> 06:08.000
And he now had no hair at all

06:10.000 --> 06:12.950
Jonathan and Martha Kent were on their way home

06:13.000 --> 06:16.950
Suddenly, a meteor hit the road behind them

06:17.000 --> 06:18.950
What was that, Jonathan?

06:19.000 --> 06:20.950
Asked Martha

06:21.000 --> 06:22.950
What's happening?

06:23.000 --> 06:24.950
Boom!

06:25.000 --> 06:27.950
A spaceship crashed into the road in front of them

06:28.000 --> 06:30.950
Jonathan tried to stop the car

06:31.000 --> 06:33.950
But it crashed into a cornfield

06:34.000 --> 06:35.950
When they opened their eyes

06:36.000 --> 06:37.950
They saw a boy

06:38.000 --> 06:39.950
He was about three years old

06:40.000 --> 06:42.950
And he had no clothes

06:43.000 --> 06:45.950
The boy pulled Jonathan's car door

06:46.000 --> 06:46.950
It opened

06:47.000 --> 06:49.950
Then he pulled Martha's car door

06:50.000 --> 06:51.950
It opened too

06:52.000 --> 06:55.950
Martha and Jonathan were very surprised

06:56.000 --> 06:57.950
They were soon out of the car

06:58.000 --> 07:00.950
Martha took the boy in her arms

07:01.000 --> 07:02.950
Are you okay?

07:03.000 --> 07:03.950
Asked Jonathan

07:04.000 --> 07:05.950
Yes, I'm fine

07:06.000 --> 07:08.950
You? said Martha

07:09.000 --> 07:12.950
But yes, children don't fall from the sky

07:13.000 --> 07:14.950
Jonathan said

07:15.000 --> 07:17.950
Then, where did he come from?

07:18.000 --> 07:18.950
Martha asked

07:19.000 --> 07:22.950
I don't think his mum and dad are from Kansas

07:23.000 --> 07:24.950
We can't keep him, Martha

07:25.000 --> 07:26.950
Said Jonathan

07:27.000 --> 07:28.950
What can we say to people?

07:29.000 --> 07:31.950
We found him in a cornfield?

07:32.000 --> 07:34.950
We didn't find him, Jonathan

07:35.000 --> 07:36.950
Said Martha

07:37.000 --> 07:38.950
He found us

07:39.000 --> 07:53.950
Chapter 2

07:54.000 --> 07:57.950
Special and Different

07:58.000 --> 08:00.950
Jonathan and Martha took the boy home to their farm

08:01.000 --> 08:03.950
They named him Clark

08:04.000 --> 08:06.950
They didn't tell him about his arrival

08:07.000 --> 08:09.950
They didn't tell other people either

08:10.000 --> 08:12.950
If someone asked, they said

08:13.000 --> 08:14.950
He's Martha's sister's son

08:15.000 --> 08:16.950
She died

08:17.000 --> 08:20.950
They didn't want Clark to be different from other children

08:21.000 --> 08:22.950
But he was different

08:23.000 --> 08:24.950
He was special

08:25.000 --> 08:26.950
He was very strong

08:27.000 --> 08:28.950
He was very fast

08:29.000 --> 08:30.950
Nothing hurt him

08:31.000 --> 08:32.950
When he was eight

08:33.000 --> 08:34.950
A big milk can hit his head

08:35.000 --> 08:37.950
It didn't hurt him

08:38.000 --> 08:43.950
2001, Smallville, Kansas, USA

08:44.000 --> 08:45.950
Clark sat at his computer

08:46.000 --> 08:48.950
Every morning he used the internet

08:49.000 --> 08:52.950
He wanted to find stories about special people

08:53.000 --> 08:54.950
Very strong people

08:55.000 --> 08:56.950
Very fast people

08:57.000 --> 08:58.950
Clark Kent, Martha called

08:59.000 --> 09:01.950
You're going to be late for the bus

09:02.000 --> 09:03.950
Okay, I'm coming

09:04.000 --> 09:05.950
Shouted Clark

09:06.000 --> 09:07.950
He put on his school clothes and shoes

09:08.000 --> 09:11.950
Cleaned his room and put his school books in his bag

09:12.000 --> 09:13.950
All in one minute

09:14.000 --> 09:17.950
Martha came into his room with some clothes

09:18.000 --> 09:21.950
You can wear these to the homecoming dance this weekend

09:22.000 --> 09:22.950
She said

09:23.000 --> 09:24.950
I'm not going, Mum

09:25.000 --> 09:25.950
Said Clark

09:26.000 --> 09:30.950
I haven't got a girl to go with Did you ask anyone?

09:31.000 --> 09:32.950
Martha asked

09:33.000 --> 09:34.950
No, he said

09:35.000 --> 09:36.950
He ran down to the kitchen

09:37.000 --> 09:38.950
What's that letter, son?

09:39.000 --> 09:40.950
Ask Jonathan

09:41.000 --> 09:42.950
It's for the football team

09:43.000 --> 09:44.950
Said Clark

09:45.000 --> 09:46.950
They want some new players

09:47.000 --> 09:48.950
You can't do it

09:49.000 --> 09:50.950
Said Jonathan

09:51.000 --> 09:52.950
Oh, please Dad

09:53.000 --> 09:53.950
Said Clark

09:54.000 --> 09:54.950
I can run slowly

09:55.000 --> 09:56.950
I can be careful

09:57.000 --> 09:58.950
I'm sorry Clark

09:59.000 --> 10:00.950
Said Jonathan

10:01.000 --> 10:04.950
But the answer is no I don't want to be different

10:05.000 --> 10:06.950
Shouted Clark

10:07.000 --> 10:08.950
I can never do normal things

10:09.000 --> 10:10.950
People at school think I'm a loser

10:11.000 --> 10:12.950
He ran out of the door

10:13.000 --> 10:16.950
We must tell him about the spaceship

10:17.000 --> 10:18.950
Martha said to Jonathan

10:19.000 --> 10:21.950
Clark walked to the bus stop

10:22.000 --> 10:23.950
He was late again

10:24.000 --> 10:26.950
The school bus drove off without him

10:27.000 --> 10:28.950
Oh no, he said

10:29.000 --> 10:30.950
Everything's going wrong today

10:31.000 --> 10:32.950
Suddenly

10:33.000 --> 10:34.950
He smiled a big smile

10:35.000 --> 10:37.950
He turned and ran through the field

10:38.000 --> 10:40.950
At a hundred kilometers an hour

10:41.000 --> 10:43.950
The bus arrived at school

10:44.000 --> 10:47.950
Clark's friends Pete Ross and Chloe Sullivan were on it

10:48.000 --> 10:50.950
Chloe was new in Smallville

10:51.000 --> 10:53.950
Her dad worked at Luther Corps

10:54.000 --> 10:55.950
She wrote for the school newspaper

10:56.000 --> 10:57.950
And took photos for it

10:58.000 --> 11:00.950
She was always ready with her camera

11:01.000 --> 11:03.950
Are you going to the dance with anyone?

11:04.000 --> 11:05.950
Pete asked Chloe

11:06.000 --> 11:07.950
No, not yet

11:08.000 --> 11:09.950
Said Chloe

11:10.000 --> 11:12.950
Well, if Clark doesn't ask you

11:13.000 --> 11:15.950
I'm not interested in Clark Pete

11:16.000 --> 11:17.950
She said

11:18.000 --> 11:18.950
Right

11:19.000 --> 11:20.950
Said Pete

11:21.000 --> 11:22.950
He knew that wasn't true

11:23.000 --> 11:26.950
Well, we can go to the dance together if you want

11:27.000 --> 11:27.950
He said

11:28.000 --> 11:29.950
Not boy and girl

11:30.000 --> 11:31.950
Friend and friend

11:32.000 --> 11:33.950
Suddenly Clark was there

11:34.000 --> 11:35.950
Hi you too

11:36.000 --> 11:36.950
He said

11:37.000 --> 11:40.950
Pete and Chloe were very surprised to see their friend

11:41.000 --> 11:42.950
We saw you at your farm

11:43.000 --> 11:43.950
Chloe said

11:44.000 --> 11:45.950
You weren't on the bus

11:46.000 --> 11:48.950
I came a different way

11:49.000 --> 11:49.950
Said Clark

11:50.000 --> 11:52.950
Are you ready for the football team Clark?

11:53.000 --> 11:53.950
Asked Pete

11:54.000 --> 11:55.950
I'm not going to do it

11:56.000 --> 11:57.950
Said Clark

11:58.000 --> 11:59.950
But Clark said Pete

12:00.000 --> 12:02.950
Do you want to be the scarecrow?

12:03.000 --> 12:04.950
The scarecrow

12:05.000 --> 12:06.950
Chloe said loudly

12:07.000 --> 12:08.950
What's the scarecrow?

12:09.000 --> 12:09.950
Shh

12:10.000 --> 12:10.950
Said Pete

12:11.000 --> 12:12.950
This happens here every year Chloe

12:13.000 --> 12:14.950
Before the homecoming game

12:15.000 --> 12:17.950
The football players choose someone

12:18.000 --> 12:19.950
A loser

12:20.000 --> 12:21.950
They take him to the cornfield

12:22.000 --> 12:23.950
And take all his clothes

12:24.000 --> 12:27.950
Then they write a big red S on the front of his body

12:28.000 --> 12:30.950
And they put him on a big wooden pole

12:31.000 --> 12:31.950
Said Clark

12:32.000 --> 12:34.950
So He's a scarecrow

12:35.000 --> 12:35.950
How terrible

12:36.000 --> 12:37.950
Said Chloe

12:38.000 --> 12:40.950
Then Clark saw a beautiful girl

12:41.000 --> 12:43.950
With long brown hair and a lovely smile

12:44.000 --> 12:45.950
See you later

12:46.000 --> 12:47.950
He said to his friends

12:48.000 --> 12:51.950
Clark walked across to Lana Lang

12:52.000 --> 12:55.950
He was a meter from her Suddenly he crashed to the ground

12:56.000 --> 12:57.950
His books went everywhere

12:58.000 --> 13:01.950
Why does this always happen near Lana?

13:02.000 --> 13:02.950
He thought

13:03.000 --> 13:04.950
Is it because I like her?

13:05.000 --> 13:06.950
Hi Clark

13:07.000 --> 13:07.950
Are you okay?

13:08.000 --> 13:08.950
She asked

13:09.000 --> 13:10.950
Hi Lana

13:11.000 --> 13:11.950
He said

13:12.000 --> 13:12.950
Yeah

13:13.000 --> 13:13.950
I'm fine

13:14.000 --> 13:15.950
She gave his books to him

13:16.000 --> 13:17.950
You're reading Nietzsche, huh?

13:18.000 --> 13:19.950
Are you man or Superman?

13:20.000 --> 13:21.950
I don't know

13:22.000 --> 13:22.950
Clark said

13:23.000 --> 13:24.950
They smiled

13:25.000 --> 13:26.950
Lana

13:27.000 --> 13:28.950
shouted Whitney Fordman

13:29.000 --> 13:30.950
A tall good looking student

13:31.000 --> 13:32.950
He was Lana's boyfriend

13:33.000 --> 13:35.950
Whitney was fantastic at sports

13:36.000 --> 13:37.950
He was in all the school teams

13:38.000 --> 13:40.950
He ran up and kissed Lana

13:41.000 --> 13:43.000
They walked away together

13:44.000 --> 13:44.950
Chapter 3

13:45.000 --> 13:45.950
Two terrible shocks

13:46.000 --> 13:47.950
A student looked at the photos of the school sports teams

13:48.000 --> 13:50.950
He looked at the 1989 photo

13:51.000 --> 13:54.950
You're late for your class young man?

13:55.000 --> 14:02.950
Said a student

14:03.000 --> 14:05.950
He looked at the 1989 photo

14:06.000 --> 14:08.950
You're late for your class young man?

14:09.000 --> 14:10.950
Said a student

14:11.000 --> 14:12.950
A class young man?

14:13.000 --> 14:14.950
Said a teacher behind him

14:15.000 --> 14:15.950
The student turned

14:16.000 --> 14:17.950
What's your name?

14:18.000 --> 14:18.950
Asked the teacher

14:19.000 --> 14:20.950
Are you new?

14:21.000 --> 14:24.950
Suddenly the student hit the teacher in the face

14:25.000 --> 14:27.950
A big blue electric shock

14:28.000 --> 14:28.950
Went from the student's hand

14:29.000 --> 14:30.950
Into the teacher's body

14:31.000 --> 14:33.950
The teacher crashed into the wall

14:34.000 --> 14:37.950
The student took the photo of the three happy football players

14:38.000 --> 14:39.950
And left the school

14:40.000 --> 14:41.950
I'm gonna get you

14:42.000 --> 14:43.950
He thought

14:44.000 --> 14:46.950
Lex Luthor drove his Porsche through the country

14:47.000 --> 14:49.950
To the Luther Court factory in Smallville

14:50.000 --> 14:53.950
The Smallville factory doesn't make any money

14:54.000 --> 14:55.950
Lionel Luthor said to his son

14:56.000 --> 14:57.950
Go to Smallville

14:58.000 --> 14:59.950
Make changes

15:00.000 --> 15:01.950
So Lex left Metropolis

15:02.000 --> 15:05.950
And here he was In the centre of nowhere

15:06.000 --> 15:07.950
Great

15:08.000 --> 15:09.950
Lex arrived at Luther Court

15:10.000 --> 15:11.950
He was 21 years old

15:12.000 --> 15:15.950
And he still had no hair

15:16.000 --> 15:17.950
He walked into the factory

15:18.000 --> 15:21.950
A man sat at a desk with his lunch

15:22.000 --> 15:24.950
Mr. Luthor, the man said surprised

15:25.000 --> 15:27.950
My name's Gabe Sullivan

15:28.000 --> 15:29.950
Call me Lex

15:30.000 --> 15:31.950
The workers aren't happy Lex

15:32.000 --> 15:33.950
Said Gabe

15:34.000 --> 15:36.000
They're frightened about their jobs

15:37.000 --> 15:38.950
It's okay, said Lex

15:39.000 --> 15:41.000
I want everyone to stay

15:42.000 --> 15:43.950
But your father said

15:44.000 --> 15:45.950
I'm not my father

15:46.000 --> 15:48.000
Said Lex Luthor

15:50.000 --> 15:52.950
Later, Lex drove down a small country road

15:53.000 --> 15:54.950
At a hundred kilometers an hour

15:55.000 --> 15:58.000
His car radio played loud music

15:59.000 --> 16:01.950
Not far away, Clark was on a bridge

16:02.000 --> 16:04.000
He looked into the water

16:05.000 --> 16:06.950
He thought about his life

16:07.000 --> 16:08.950
And he wasn't happy

16:09.000 --> 16:11.000
He didn't hear Lex Luthor's car

16:13.000 --> 16:14.950
Lex answered his mobile phone

16:15.000 --> 16:17.950
He didn't look at the road for a minute

16:18.000 --> 16:19.950
He drove onto the bridge

16:20.000 --> 16:21.950
Then he saw Clark

16:22.000 --> 16:23.950
He tried to stop the car

16:24.000 --> 16:25.950
But Clark was right in front of him

16:26.000 --> 16:27.950
I'm going to hit him

16:28.000 --> 16:29.950
Lex thought

16:30.000 --> 16:31.950
Their eyes met

16:32.000 --> 16:33.950
Lex's car crashed into Clark

16:34.000 --> 16:35.950
Boom

16:36.000 --> 16:38.950
The car and Clark went over the bridge

16:39.000 --> 16:40.950
And into the water

16:41.000 --> 16:42.950
Clark's eyes closed

16:43.000 --> 16:45.000
